# Project-specific
# datasets/raw/ is committed: 977 KB, static, read-only, and the source of truth for
# `dvc repro`. Only derived artifacts are ignored — DVC owns them as stage outputs.
datasets/processed/
datasets/interim/
mlruns/
mlflow.db
optuna.db
mlartifacts/
# reports/ is inverted, not blanket-ignored: most dvc.yaml stage outs with
# cache: false (metrics_summary.json, decile_lift.csv, promotion_decision.json)
# are small, deterministic, and meant to be git-tracked directly.
# test_predictions.parquet is a cached out instead — a real per-row data
# artifact (1,409 rows), not a small aggregate, so it belongs with the other
# cached parquets (split_manifest.parquet, telco_churn_features.parquet), not
# the receipts. Only human-only dumps and the local mirrors of MLflow-owned
# artifacts (reports/ is not their source of truth) stay ignored.
reports/figures/
reports/validation/
reports/feature_discovery/
reports/dev_oof_predictions.parquet
reports/dev_shap_values.parquet
reports/metrics.json
reports/economics.json
reports/error_analysis.json
reports/drift_reference.json
reports/model_card.json
reports/promotion_review.json
# The six *_receipt.json files (ingest, validation, train, calibrate, eval,
# error_analysis) are the exception to "receipts are git-tracked" above.
# Git-committing a cache: false out defeats DVC's own missing-output check:
# a fresh clone would inherit a hash-matching receipt for a Postgres/MLflow
# pair that doesn't actually exist yet, so `dvc repro` reports the ingest/
# train/calibrate/evaluate/error_analysis stages up to date against infra
# that has never been touched (see CLAUDE.md's Data Handling section). Left
# gitignored, a fresh clone has no receipt on disk, DVC sees the out missing,
# and the whole chain reruns for real — no manual --force workaround needed.
reports/ingest_receipt.json
reports/validation_receipt.json
reports/train_receipt.json
reports/calibrate_receipt.json
reports/eval_receipt.json
reports/error_analysis_receipt.json
.dvc/cache/
project_thoughts.md
prompts.txt
summary.md
